      "writtenOn": "2024-09-16T22:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "go/android-ndk-api-guidelines#methods-with-non-trivial-error-possibilities\n\nDo you think these count as \"the only error possibility is the result of a trivial check\"? For simple programming errors we usually lean toward just using `abort()` instead of returning error codes, but it\u0027s definitely subjective.",
